WEBVTT

00:00:58.565 --> 00:01:03.157
As many as 16,000 fibers 
will festoon a single seed,

00:01:03.157 --> 00:01:07.530
bulging from the seed’s surface 
like miniature water balloons.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:10.750
Each cotton fiber, 
no matter how large it grows,

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:13.185
is made of just one cell.

00:01:13.185 --> 00:01:16.975
That cell has multiple layers 
of cell wall.

00:01:16.975 --> 00:01:20.115
After a few days, 
the sides of the first layer,

00:01:20.115 --> 00:01:22.245
called the primary cell wall,

00:01:22.245 --> 00:01:25.605
stiffen, pushing cell growth 
in one direction

00:01:25.605 --> 00:01:28.575
and causing the fiber to elongate.

00:01:28.575 --> 00:01:32.345
The fiber elongates 
quickly for about 16 days.